# Travlr Getaways - CS499 Milestone Three Enhancement

## Artifact Overview

Travlr Getaways is a full-stack travel application originally developed during CS465 Full Stack Development.

The application uses an Angular administrative interface, an Express backend API, and MongoDB database integration to manage travel information.

For CS499 Computer Science Capstone, this artifact was enhanced to demonstrate improvements in algorithms and data structures.

---

# Enhancements Completed

## 1. Trip Search Functionality

A dynamic search feature was added to the administrator dashboard.

Administrators can now search trips based on:

- Trip name
- Resort location
- Trip description

This enhancement uses filtering logic to process stored trip data and return matching results.

---

## 2. Trip Sorting Functionality

Sorting capabilities were added to allow administrators to organize trip information.

Available sorting options include:

- Name (A-Z)
- Name (Z-A)
- Price (Low to High)
- Price (High to Low)

This enhancement demonstrates comparison-based sorting and data transformation.

---

## 3. Administrator Dashboard Improvements

The administrative interface was redesigned to improve usability.

Improvements include:

- Updated dashboard layout
- Improved trip cards
- Better organization of trip information
- Improved user interaction

